{"httpRequest":{"body":{"inputs":"Software Requirements Specification (SRS)     For AI-Powered Talent Bridge Platform     Version 1. 0   ---       1.  Introduction          1. 1 Purpose   This document outlines the requirements for an AI-driven platform that connects students with job opportunities, optimizes resumes, and provides universities with actionable insights.  The system aims to bridge the gap between education and employment while ensuring financial sustainability. 2 Scope   The platform will: - Aggregate student data from multiple colleges into a centralized database.  - Use AI ML for resume optimization, candidate matching, and trend analysis.  - Enable employers to post internships jobs and search for candidates.  - Provide universities with dashboards to identify skill gaps and design training programs.  - Implement monetization models (subscriptions, premium features). 3 Definitions   -   AI ML  : Artificial Intelligence Machine Learning.  -   GDPR  : General Data Protection Regulation (data privacy compliance).  -   Stakeholders  : Students, universities, employers.  ---       2.  Overall Description          2. 1 Product Perspective   The platform operates as a standalone web application with integrations for college databases, third-party authentication (e.  LinkedIn), and payment gateways. 2 User Classes   1.    Students  : Create profiles, build resumes, apply for jobs, and track progress.    Employers  : Post jobs, search candidates, purchase premium features.    Universities  : Access dashboards, analyze skill gaps, and manage training programs.    Admins  : Oversee system operations, user management, and revenue streams. 3 Operating Environment   -   Frontend  : Web-based (React. js Angular) with mobile-responsive design.  -   Backend  : Node. js Python (Django Flask).  -   Database  : PostgreSQL MongoDB (scalable, encrypted).  -   Cloud  : AWS Google Cloud for deployment.  ---       3.  System Features          3. 1 Centralized Database System   -   FR1  : Aggregate student data (skills, certifications, employment history) from multiple colleges.  -   FR2  : Implement role-based access control (RBAC) for data security.  -   FR3  : Offer subscription tiers for employers (e.  premium search filters). 2 AI Resume Builder   -   FR4  : Generate resumes using templates tailored to industry standards.  -   FR5  : Auto-update resumes based on new skills certifications.  -   FR6  : Provide AI feedback on resume strength (e.  keyword optimization). 3 Candidate Matching   -   FR7  : Use ML algorithms to match candidates with jobs based on skills, experience, and preferences.  -   FR8  : Enable predictive analytics for career path recommendations. 4 Internship   Placement Module   -   FR9  : Allow employers to post internships jobs with automated application tracking.  -   FR10  : Track student placement outcomes and employer feedback. 5 University Dashboard   -   FR11  : Display skill gap analytics and industry trends.  -   FR12  : Enable universities to design training programs via subscription-based insights. 6 Financial Sustainability   -   FR13  : Monetize via employer subscriptions, university analytics subscriptions, and student premium tools (e.  advanced resume templates).  ---       4.  External Interface Requirements          4. 1 User Interfaces   -   UI1  : Student dashboard with resume builder, job listings, and progress tracking.  -   UI2  : Employer portal with job posting, candidate search, and analytics.  -   UI3  : University dashboard with heatmaps of skill gaps and training recommendations. 2 APIs   -   API1  : Integration with LinkedIn Google for profile authentication.  -   API2  : Payment gateway integration (Stripe PayPal).  ---       5.  Non-Functional Requirements   -   NFR1  : System response time   2 seconds for search queries.  -   NFR2  : GDPR-compliant data encryption (at rest and in transit).  -   NFR3  : Scalability to support 10,000  concurrent users.  -   NFR4  : 99. 9  uptime with automated backups.  ---       6.  Other Requirements          6. 1 Legal   - Compliance with data privacy laws (GDPR, CCPA). 2 Glossary   -   Predictive Analytics  : Forecasting future trends using historical data.  -   RBAC  : Role-Based Access Control.  ---   Approval   Prepared by:  Your Name  Reviewed by:  Lab Instructor s Name  Date:  DD MM YYYY  --- This SRS document provides a structured blueprint for developing the AI-Powered Talent Bridge platform, aligning with the hackathon s objectives and ensuring scalability, security, and sustainability"},"headers":{"Content-Type":"application/json","User-Agent":"@huggingface/inference/4.9.0 Node.js/22"},"method":"POST","url":"https://router.huggingface.co/hf-inference/models/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2/pipeline/feature-extraction"},"httpResponse":{"body":"","requestId":"","status":401},"level":"error","message":"Failed to generate embedding: Failed to perform inference: an HTTP error occurred when requesting the provider","name":"ProviderApiError","service":"team-memory-backend","stack":"ProviderApiError: Failed to perform inference: an HTTP error occurred when requesting the provider\n    at innerRequest (D:\\Charaha\\backend\\node_modules\\@huggingface\\inference\\dist\\commonjs\\utils\\request.js:66:15)\n    at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:105:5)\n    at async featureExtraction (D:\\Charaha\\backend\\node_modules\\@huggingface\\inference\\dist\\commonjs\\tasks\\nlp\\featureExtraction.js:13:27)\n    at async VectorService.generateEmbedding (D:\\Charaha\\backend\\src\\services\\vector.service.js:45:24)\n    at async VectorService.storeVector (D:\\Charaha\\backend\\src\\services\\vector.service.js:59:25)\n    at async ingestFiles (D:\\Charaha\\backend\\src\\controllers\\google-drive.controller.js:103:11)","timestamp":"2025-09-29T07:30:09.376Z"}
